  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Grandpa and Tom walk in the street. They want to see a big ship. They stop at a sign. It says: \"Ship. This way.\" \"The ship is there,\" says Grandpa. Tom looks and smiles. The ship is white and blue. It is very big. It is next to the sea.",
      "Then Tom sees a new sign. It says: \"No dogs.\" \"Pip can't come here,\" says Tom. \"No, he can't,\" says Grandpa. \"He is at home with Mom.\" Tom sees a sign on a post. It says: \"Don't run.\" Tom walks with Grandpa. \"Is the ship fun?\" asks Tom. \"Yes, it is!\" says Grandpa.",
      "There is a small shop next to the ship. The sign says: \"Open.\" Grandpa gets a juice for Tom. Tom looks at the big ship. He has a big smile. \"I like ships,\" says Tom. \"Where is the ship going?\" \"I don't know,\" says Grandpa. They look at the sea and smile."
    ],
    "summary": "Grandpa and Tom walk to see a big ship at the sea. They read four signs on the way.",
